    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Company:  {{ $json.company }}\n\nAnnouncements: {{ JSON.stringify($json.announcements) }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a senior market-analyst preparing a weekly competitive-research brief.\n\n**INPUT**\nA JSON array named \"announcements\" that contains recent LinkedIn posts from the company.\n\n**TASK**\nExtract only the information requested below, using the input content.\n\n**RETURN** *exactly and only* the following four data fields in a single JSON object (no extra keys, no narrative prose):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"current_positioning_and_message\": \"string\",\n  \"recent_launches\": [\n    \"bullet 1\",\n    \"bullet 2\"\n  ],\n  \"recent_major_product_releases\": [\n    \"bullet 1\",\n    \"bullet 2\"\n  ],\n  \"recent_funding_or_customer_announcements\": [\n    \"bullet 1\",\n    \"bullet 2\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Formatting notes**\n\n* Use concise sentences; include dates / figures when available.\n* Keep bullet arrays empty (`[]`) if no items exist, or include the \"No public information found\" note.\n* Do not add any other section, commentary, or formatting outside the JSON object."
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -336,
        608
      ],
      "id": "e4c6e7f3-7325-4c49-b079-fe04fed38ff5",
      "name": "Analysis"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Company:  {{ $json.company }}\n\n{{ $json.posts.join('\\n\\n') }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You will receive one variable named **posts**.\nIt is a JSON array of recent LinkedIn post objects from a single company.\nEach post object contains at least these keys:\n\n. id          - string\n. content     - full post text (may include emojis, hashtags, links)\n. created_at  - ISO date-time string\n. permalink   - URL of the post\n\nTASK\nFrom that list, identify every post that CLEARLY does one of the following:\n\n1. Announces a new product or major feature launch / release\n2. Announces a pricing change or new pricing tier\n3. Announces an acquisition, merger, or large strategic partnership\n4. Announces a major hiring initiative or expansion (e.g. \"we’re hiring 100…\")\n5. Announces a funding / investment round, customer win, or large contract\n\nIgnore general thought-leadership, memes, minor bug fixes, or vague \"big things coming\" teasers unless they include a concrete launch date or feature name.\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn **exactly one** JSON object with a single key **\"announcements\"**.\nThat key’s value must be an array (which may be empty).\nEach element MUST follow this schema exactly:\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"Product Launch | Feature Launch | Pricing | Hiring | Acquisition | Merger | Partnership | Funding | Customer Win\",\n  \"title\": \"Short headline (≤ 12 words, no emojis)\",\n  \"description\": \"One clear sentence that summarises WHAT happened and, if available, WHEN and HOW MUCH (dates, $ figures, etc.)\"\n}\n\nRules\n• Do NOT wrap the output in triple back-ticks or any other markup.\n• Keep the array empty (\"announcements\": []) if no qualifying posts exist.\n• Do not invent or infer information that is not explicitly in the post.\n• If content is duplicated across several posts, keep only one entry for it.\n• Preserve numerals, currency symbols, and dates exactly as written.\n\n"
        }
      },
